=== MODEL ===
This one splits p into three parts: prefix, middle, suffix. For each occurrence start of the prefix at i, find the first occurrence of the middle at j ≥ i+len(prefix), then the first occurrence of the suffix at k ≥ j+len(middle). Length = k + len(suffix) − i. I'll use `str.find` for the search, which is fine for correctness here.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-6114", "code": "class Solution:\n    def shortestMatchingSubstring(self, s: str, p: str) -> int:\n        pre, suf = p.split('*', 1)\n        mid, suf = suf.split('*', 1)\n        # pre, mid, suf: literal parts. Find occurrences greedily.\n        n = len(s)\n        best = -1\n        # Precompute occurrences of each part\n        def occurrences(t):\n            res = []\n            if t == \"\":\n                return list(range(n + 1))\n            start = s.find(t)\n            while start != -1:\n                res.append(start)\n                start = s.find(t, start + 1)\n            return res\n        pre_occ = occurrences(pre)\n        mid_occ = occurrences(mid)\n        suf_occ = occurrences(suf)\n        import bisect\n        for i in pre_occ:\n            # earliest mid start >= i + len(pre)\n            idx = bisect.bisect_left(mid_occ, i + len(pre))\n            if idx == len(mid_occ):\n                continue\n            j = mid_occ[idx]\n            idx2 = bisect.bisect_left(suf_occ, j + len(mid))\n            if idx2 == len(suf_occ):\n                continue\n            k = suf_occ[idx2]\n            length = k + len(suf) - i\n            if best == -1 or length < best:\n                best = length\n        return best\n"}

