class Solution:
    def generateString(self, str1: str, str2: str) -> str:


=== MODEL ===
This is the "generate string" problem (LeetCode 3474 style). My plan:

1. Length L = n + m - 1. Positions fixed by 'T' constraints must equal str2 at each offset; conflicts among overlapping T-windows mean no solution.
2. Unfixed positions start as wildcards, initialized to 'a'.
3. For each 'F' window not already forced to differ by a fixed character, we must change one of its unfixed positions to something other than the str2 character. Greedily pick the last unfixed position in that window and set it to 'a' or 'b' (whichever differs from the required character) — this keeps the string lexicographically smallest.
4. Verify all 'F' windows are not equal to str2; if any fails, return "".

I'll submit this implementation.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-8397", "code": "class Solution:\n    def generateString(self, str1: str, str2: str) -> str:\n        n, m = len(str1), len(str2)\n        L = n + m - 1\n        word = [None] * L      # fixed characters\n        fixed = [False] * L\n\n        # Apply 'T' constraints.\n        for i, c in enumerate(str1):\n            if c == 'T':\n                for j in range(m):\n                    p = i + j\n                    if fixed[p]:\n                        if word[p] != str2[j]:\n                            return \"\"\n                    else:\n                        fixed[p] = True\n                        word[p] = str2[j]\n\n        # Fill unfixed positions with 'a' initially.\n        for p in range(L):\n            if not fixed[p]:\n                word[p] = 'a'\n\n        # Handle 'F' constraints: each window must differ from str2.\n        for i, c in enumerate(str1):\n            if c != 'F':\n                continue\n            # Check if already differs due to a fixed position.\n            def matches():\n                for j in range(m):\n                    if word[i + j] != str2[j]:\n                        return False\n                return True\n            if not matches():\n                continue\n            # Find the last unfixed position in the window to modify.\n            changed = False\n            for j in range(m - 1, -1, -1):\n                p = i + j\n                if not fixed[p]:\n                    # set to a character different from str2[j], smallest possible\n                    # (word[p] currently 'a' or possibly modified before)\n                    for cand in 'ab':\n                        if cand != str2[j]:\n                            word[p] = cand\n                            break\n                    changed = True\n                    break\n            if not changed:\n                return \"\"\n\n        # Final verification.\n        for i, c in enumerate(str1):\n            window_equal = all(word[i + j] == str2[j] for j in range(m))\n            if c == 'T' and not window_equal:\n                return \"\"\n            if c == 'F' and window_equal:\n                return \"\"\n\n        return \"\".join(word)\n"}

