cost.length == nums.length
1 <= nums[i], cost[i] <= 1000
1 <= k <= 1000

Starter code:

class Solution:
    def minimumCost(self, nums: List[int], cost: List[int], k: int) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
This is a DP with the number of subarrays used as the extra dimension. Let P[r] be the prefix sum of nums and C[r] the prefix sum of cost. If the i-th subarray is nums[l..r], its cost is (P[r] + k·i)·(C[r] − C[l−1]). Expanding gives P[r]·(C[r]−C[l−1]) + k·i·(C[r]−C[l−1]), which couples the subarray index i with the segment, so the state needs the count of subarrays so far. That makes it O(n²·n) naively, which is too slow at n = 1000.

The key observation is that the index i multiplies the segment cost, so instead of tracking i explicitly, I can use the standard trick: the total is sum over segments of (P[r] + k·i)·segcost. Since k·i·segcost = k·(number of segments before and including this one)·segcost, I can rewrite it as a DP over prefixes where dp[j][i] = min cost to cover the first j elements with i segments. That is O(n²·n) = 10⁹ in the worst case, which is still too slow in Python, so I use Convex Hull Trick: for a fixed i, the transition dp[r][i] = min over l of (dp[l−1][i−1] + P[r]·(C[r]−C[l−1]) + k·i·(C[r]−C[l−1])) is linear in (C[r]+ ... ) terms, enabling a per-layer convex hull optimization in O(n) per layer, giving O(n²) overall.

I'll implement the layered DP with a monotone-slope convex hull for each i.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-7649", "code": "from typing import List\n\nclass Solution:\n    def minimumCost(self, nums: List[int], cost: List[int], k: int) -> int:\n        n = len(nums)\n        P = [0] * (n + 1)  # prefix sums of nums\n        C = [0] * (n + 1)  # prefix sums of cost\n        for i in range(n):\n            P[i + 1] = P[i] + nums[i]\n            C[i + 1] = C[i] + cost[i]\n        INF = float('inf')\n\n        # dp_prev[j]: min cost to cover first j elements with (i-1) segments.\n        # Transition for segment index i ending at r, starting after l (prefix l):\n        #   dp_cur[r] = min_l dp_prev[l] + (P[r] + k*i) * (C[r] - C[l])\n        #             = min_l [dp_prev[l] - (P[r] + k*i)*C[l]] + (P[r] + k*i)*C[r]\n        # For fixed i, this is a min over lines f_l(x) = m_l * x + b_l with\n        # m_l = -C[l], b_l = dp_prev[l], evaluated at x = P[r] + k*i.\n        # Slopes -C[l] are decreasing in l (C increasing), queries x increasing in r.\n        dp_prev = [INF] * (n + 1)\n        dp_prev[0] = 0\n        answer = INF\n        for i in range(1, n + 1):\n            dp_cur = [INF] * (n + 1)\n            # Monotone CHT: lines added with decreasing slopes, queries increasing x -> min.\n            hull_m = []\n            hull_b = []\n            hull_ptr = 0\n\n            def bad(m1, b1, m2, b2, m3, b3):\n                # True if line 2 is unnecessary given lines 1 and 3 (slopes m1 > m2 > m3)\n                return (b3 - b1) * (m1 - m2) <= (b2 - b1) * (m1 - m3)\n\n            for r in range(i, n + 1):\n                # Add line for l = r-1 if reachable\n                l = r - 1\n                if dp_prev[l] < INF:\n                    m_new = -C[l]\n                    b_new = dp_prev[l]\n                    while len(hull_m) >= 2 and bad(hull_m[-2], hull_b[-2],\n                                                   hull_m[-1], hull_b[-1],\n                                                   m_new, b_new):\n                        hull_m.pop()\n                        hull_b.pop()\n                        if hull_ptr > len(hull_m):\n                            hull_ptr = len(hull_m)\n                    hull_m.append(m_new)\n                    hull_b.append(b_new)\n                if not hull_m:\n                    continue\n                x = P[r] + k * i\n                # advance pointer while next line is better at x\n                if hull_ptr >= len(hull_m):\n                    hull_ptr = len(hull_m) - 1\n                while hull_ptr + 1 < len(hull_m) and \\\n                        hull_m[hull_ptr + 1] * x + hull_b[hull_ptr + 1] <= \\\n                        hull_m[hull_ptr] * x + hull_b[hull_ptr]:\n                    hull_ptr += 1\n                best = hull_m[hull_ptr] * x + hull_b[hull_ptr]\n                dp_cur[r] = best + x * C[r]\n            dp_prev = dp_cur\n            if dp_prev[n] < answer:\n                answer = dp_prev[n]\n        return int(answer)\n"}

